  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Comparatives and Superlatives",
      "content": "Compare people, things, and ideas using comparatives and superlatives.\n\nComparative (more/less/as... as):\n- más... que = more... than\n- menos... que = less... than\n- tan... como = as... as\n\nSuperlative (the most/the least):\n- el/la más... = the most...\n- el/la menos... = the least...\n\nIrregular comparatives:\n- bueno → mejor (better than)\n- malo → peor (worse than)\n- grande → mayor (older/greater than)\n- pequeño → menor (younger/lesser than)\n\nFor age comparisons, mayor/menor are used instead of más/menos grande/pequeño when referring to age.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Type",
          "Formula",
          "Example"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "More than",
            "más + adjective + que",
            "Madrid es más grande que Sevilla."
          ],
          [
            "Less than",
            "menos + adjective + que",
            "Este libro es menos interesante que aquel."
          ],
          [
            "As... as",
            "tan + adjective + como",
            "Ella es tan inteligente como su hermano."
          ],
          [
            "The most",
            "el/la más + adjective + (de)",
            "Él es el más alto de la clase."
          ],
          [
            "The least",
            "el/la menos + adjective + (de)",
            "Esta película es la menos divertida."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
        "Mi casa es más bonita que la tuya. (My house is prettier than yours.)",
        "Ese examen fue más difícil que el anterior. (That exam was harder than the previous one.)",
        "Mi hermano es mayor que yo. (My brother is older than me.)",
        "Ella es la más inteligente de todos. (She is the smartest of all.)"
      ],
      "aid_note": "Romanian comparatives follow the same pattern: 'mai bun' (better), 'mai frumos' (prettier), 'cel mai' (the most). Spanish 'más que' ≈ Romanian 'mai ... decât'. The irregulars (mejor, peor) are similar to Romanian 'mai bun' and 'mai rău'."
    }
  ],
  "pronunciation": [
    {
      "title": "Comparative/Superlative — Key Patterns",
      "content": "Comparative and superlative forms have distinct pronunciation:\n\n1. **más** = mahlss (with accent mark, always stressed)\n2. **menos** = MEH-nohs (stress on first syllable)\n3. **mejor** = me-HOR (better — no accent, stress on second)\n4. **peor** = pe-HOR (worse — stress on second)\n5. **más alto** = mahlss AH-ltoh (the accent on 'má' marks stress)\n6. **el más alto** = ehl mahlss AH-ltoh (superlative — the 'el' = 'ehl')\n7. **tan... como** = tahn... KOH-moh (as... as)\n\nKey distinction:\n- 'más' (more) always has an accent mark — this is a monosyllable with stress\n- 'mas' (but) has no accent — different word!\n\nThe 'll' in 'calle' = 'y' sound, but 'll' in 'calle' vs 'la' has no 'll' — it's just 'l'.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "más alto",
          "source": "mahlss AH-ltoh (taller — 'á' has accent)"
        },
        {
          "target": "el más interesante",
          "source": "ehl mahlss een-teh-REHS-n-teh (the most interesting)"
        },
        {
          "target": "tan inteligente como",
          "source": "tahn een-teh-LIH-gen-teh KOH-moh (as intelligent as)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "type": "exercise",
      "question": "Which word means 'taller' in Spanish (comparative)?",
      "options": [
        "menos alto",
        "más alto",
        "tan alto como",
        "alto"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "'Más alto' means taller (more tall). The structure is 'más + adjective + que'."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Este libro es ____ interesante que aquel.' (This book is more interesting than that one.)",
      "correct": "más",
      "explanation": "'Más interesante' — the comparative structure 'más + adjective + que.'"
    },
    {
      "type": "exercise",
      "question": "What is the irregular comparative of 'bueno'?",
      "options": [
        "más bueno",
        "bueno",
        "mejor",
        "bueno mejor"
      ],
      "correct": 2,
      "explanation": "'Mejor' is the irregular comparative of bueno (better). 'Más bueno' is sometimes used colloquially but 'mejor' is correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Ella es ____ inteligente ____ su hermano.' (She is as smart as her brother.)",
      "correct": "tan como",
      "explanation": "'Tan inteligente como' — the 'tan... como' structure for 'as... as' comparisons."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Él es el ____ alto de la clase.' (He is the tallest in the class.)",
      "correct": "más",
      "explanation": "'El más alto de la clase' — superlative structure 'el + más + adjective + de'."
    },
    {
      "type": "exercise",
      "question": "Which form do you use for age comparisons (older/younger)?",
      "options": [
        "más viejo / más nuevo",
        "mayor / menor",
        "grande / pequeño",
        "viejo / joven"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "For age, use mayor/menor: 'Él es mayor que yo' (He is older than me). 'Más viejo' is less precise for age."
    }
  ]
